WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.290
Luton, 2011: about 203,200 people.

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.230
By 2021, about 225,300.

3
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.300
In those ten years, the share of residents
born in England fell from 67.0 per

4
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.230
cent to 60.3 per cent.

5
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:24.430
Then, in November 2024, Stellantis announced
it would close the town's van plant.

6
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.870
A growing town, a changing
population, a factory leaving.

7
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.210
Why do some residents welcome
change, while others push back?

8
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.270
In this mission, you'll
map who changes land use,

9
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.370
from community groups to governments
and transnational corporations.

10
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:45.490
Then you'll compare how long-term residents
and newer arrivals see the same streets,

11
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.070
in Luton and in a second city.

12
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.850
Your mission: explain why the same change
can be welcomed by some residents and

13
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.280
resisted by others.
